# Local API (Vite proxies /api → port 3000):
# 1) Link once: pnpm vercel:link (pick team + existing/new project; do not interrupt mid-prompt)
#    Or quick new project under default team: pnpm vercel:link:quick
# 2) Sync env: vercel env pull .env.local
# 3) Terminal A: pnpm dev:api   Terminal B: pnpm dev
#
# Production: Vercel env — DATABASE_URL (or POSTGRES_URL from Neon integration; both work).
# Use Neon’s pooled URL (host contains "-pooler") for serverless. Set for Production + Preview.
# After rotating credentials, paste the NEW URL only in Vercel / .env.local — not in git.
# Bootstrap schema once: paste db/001_init.sql into Neon SQL Editor and run.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
